course: dictionary
lesson: 9701
title: Context clues: suitcase
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A suitcase is a large case with a handle, and often wheels, for carrying clothes and other things when you travel. You can often work out a word like this from the clues around it. «Her foster mum, Jan, takes one look and fetches a proper suitcase with wheels.» The wheels tell you it is something you carry on a journey.
explain: Read the sentence around the word for more clues. «Your suitcase disappears behind a rubber curtain at check-in with a paper tag on it.» A paper tag and check-in tell you that the suitcase is taken away from you at the airport, so it must be a case for travelling.
explain: Words often go together in phrases. You can pack a suitcase, unpack a suitcase, or wheel a suitcase. «On the last morning Bawheid sits on Lily's suitcase so she can't pack.» Packing needs a suitcase, so this sentence shows what a suitcase is used for.
explain: Always test your meaning. Put it in the sentence: «On the last morning Bawheid sits on Lily's large case for carrying clothes so she can't pack.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: A suitcase is a large case with a handle, and often wheels, for carrying clothes and other things when you travel.
fact: Useful phrases are pack a suitcase, unpack a suitcase, and wheel a suitcase.
fact: «Her foster mum, Jan, takes one look and fetches a proper suitcase with wheels.»
fact: At airports and stations, keep your suitcase with you, and never carry a bag for a stranger.
fact: The plural is suitcases, as in «a line of suitcases».
exercise: «On the last morning Bawheid sits on Lily's suitcase so she can't pack.» What is a suitcase? | A small purse for coins | A tiny box for toys | A kind of hat worn at the airport | *A large case with a handle, for carrying clothes when you travel
exercise: Which phrase means putting your clothes into a suitcase before a trip? | unpack a suitcase | sit on a suitcase | *pack a suitcase | wheel a suitcase
exercise: What should you do with your suitcase at an airport or station? | Hide it under a seat | *Keep it with you | Give it to a stranger to carry | Leave it alone for anyone to take
test: «Your suitcase disappears behind a rubber curtain at check-in with a paper tag on it.» What clue shows the suitcase is taken away at the airport? | It is shiny and new | It is full of sand | It is very small | *The paper tag and the check-in
test: Which word is the plural of suitcase? | *suitcases | suitcased | suitcasing | suitcase
exam: Mo says, «A suitcase is a kind of shoe.» Is he right? | *No, a suitcase is a large case with a handle for carrying clothes | Yes, you wear it on your foot | Yes, you wear it on your head | Maybe, it depends on the weather
